backend-cad-tests-dead-suite-zone — a middle band of backend-cad-tests.lisp never runs
======================================================================================

Found: 2026-07-31, while adding build-launch-argv tests for
alfe-bricscad-batch-hidden-ui.

Symptom
-------

A large contiguous band of the FiveAM tests in
autolisp-front-end/tests/backend-cad-tests.lisp is registered but is
NEVER executed by `make -C autolisp-front-end test-sbcl`
(fiveam:run 'autolisp-front-end-suite). Sabotaging an assertion in one
of these tests does NOT redden the suite (make exits 0).

Confirmed on a pristine build (all fasl caches purged) on master:

  - bricscad-emit-run-scr-...            RUNS   (early)
  - bricscad-emit-bridge-vbs-...         does NOT run
  - autocad-backend-is-registered        does NOT run
  - bricscad-build-launch-argv-batch-shape  does NOT run
  - the cad-drive-protocol-actions-* end-to-end regression tests
    (mock CAD lifecycle) — appear to be in the dead band too
  - cad-program-denotation-parsing / cad-denotation-* (end of file)  RUN

So the file's tests split into a live head + live tail with a dead
middle. The check count is identical (412) with or without the middle
tests' assertions, proving they never run.

Impact
------

These are real regression tests (VBS/argv emitters, the file-IPC
mock-CAD lifecycle, start-engine early-exit handling). They have been
silently green — a genuine coverage hole. No product bug is implied, but
the safety net for the CAD backends is smaller than it looks.

The single file has exactly one `(in-suite autolisp-front-end-suite)` at
the top and no mid-file suite/def-suite/*suite* form, so membership
should be uniform. The dead zone is likely a RUN-ORDER effect (FiveAM
orders by its own hash, not file order) — e.g. one test ERRORS mid-run
and aborts the remainder of the suite, or a cross-file duplicate test
name orphans a subset. Not yet root-caused.

To do
-----

  - Root-cause: instrument fiveam:run to log the actual executed order
    and the total member count of autolisp-front-end-suite; find the
    first non-executed member and whether an error/abort precedes it.
  - Check for duplicate `(test NAME ...)` names across the alfe test
    files (get-test is global by name; a later file would win).
  - Once fixed, re-enable + green the whole file; the argv tests added
    at the END for alfe-bricscad-batch-hidden-ui can then move back into
    the BUILD-LAUNCH-ARGV section next to the existing one.

Workaround in place
-------------------

The alfe-bricscad-batch-hidden-ui argv tests were appended at the END of
the file (the live tail), verified to run via a sabotage probe.
